> There was a problem with my installation and I solved during the weekend.
>
> Now, with the new functions, the code is returning this error:
>
> Error in !is_preemptive(.env, resource) : invalid argument type
> Called from: eval(lhs, parent, parent)

delayed_release() uses a new function, is_preemptive(), to check
whether the resource is preemptive or not, thus producing the right
sequence of activities. Therefore, you need to add your resources to
the environment *before* calling delayed_release.

>
> And the question about the independent delay is that the Shuttle and the
> driver come together to the wayback. So that makes a 10min delay on both
> resources. I think the way it is now, makes a 20min delay, with the
> resources being released at different times. I think I would need something
> like
>
> delayed_release(env,c("Shuttle","Driver_Shuttle"),10)

That won't work. You need one delayed_release for the shuttle, one for
the driver. That makes 10 min each and the resources are released at
the same time if the times are equal.

